    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Created in 1569 when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-pius-v">Pope Pius V</a> made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cosimo-i-de-medici">Cosimo I</a> de’ Medici <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-duke-of-tuscany">Grand Duke of Tuscany</a> after his conquest of Siena.</li><li>Medici Tuscany sheltered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galileo-galilei">Galileo</a>, saw the birth of opera and made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livorno">Livorno</a> a cosmopolitan free port.</li><li>Under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-habsburg-lorraine">Habsburg-Lorraine</a> grand duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leopold-ii-holy-roman-emperor">Peter Leopold</a> it abolished torture and the death penalty in 1786.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galileo-galilei">Galileo</a> named the four moons of Jupiter he discovered in 1610 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galilean-moons">Medicean Stars</a>, in honour of Grand Duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cosimo-ii-de-medici">Cosimo II</a> and his brothers.</p></aside>
    </section>

